.vscode
private-notes.txt
# NOTE ON THE .gitkeep NEGATIONS BELOW
# ValidateWorldFiles (internal/util/util.go) requires every subfolder of the
# example world _datafiles/world/default to also exist under the live world,
# and returns a HARD error at boot when one does not. Git cannot track an empty
# directory, so any folder whose contents we ignore vanishes from a fresh clone
# and the server dies before loading a single room. Each such folder therefore
# ignores its CONTENTS (trailing /*) and re-includes a tracked .gitkeep.
# Excluding the directory itself would not work: git does not descend into an
# excluded directory, so a negation for a child of it is never even considered.
_datafiles/**/users/*
!_datafiles/**/users/.gitkeep
_datafiles/**/plugin-data/*
!_datafiles/**/plugin-data/.gitkeep
**/config-overrides.yaml
**/.roundcount
**/rooms.instances
**/mobs.instances
_datafiles/**/shops/*
!_datafiles/**/shops/.gitkeep
_datafiles/**/warehouses
# Runtime living-economy state — server-maintained delivery/stock/bounty ledgers
_datafiles/**/caravans/
_datafiles/**/foragers/
_datafiles/**/crates/
_datafiles/**/bounties.yaml
# Runtime faction rep state — not committed
_datafiles/**/factions.rep
# Runtime crime log state — not committed
_datafiles/**/factions.crimes
# Runtime NPC knowledge state — not committed
_datafiles/**/knowledge/
# Runtime NPC opinion state — not committed
_datafiles/**/opinions/
# Runtime NPC fact awareness state — not committed
_datafiles/**/facts.awareness/
# Runtime NPC goal state — not committed
_datafiles/**/goals/*
!_datafiles/**/goals/.gitkeep
.worktrees/
tools/testing/reports/*.md
